-- **Retry.** `rate_limit`, `overloaded`, `network`, `timeout` and `server` retry with exponential backoff, at most 5 attempts, honouring `retryAfterMs`. `auth`, `bad_request`, `context_length` and `quota` (HTTP 402, or a 429 whose message says the plan or balance is spent) never retry. Each try is its own `attempt` event.
+- **Retry.** `rate_limit`, `overloaded`, `network`, `timeout` and `server` retry with exponential backoff, at most 5 attempts, honouring `retryAfterMs`. `auth`, `bad_request`, `context_length` and `quota` (HTTP 402, or a 429 whose message says the plan or balance is spent) never retry. A quota error that says when it comes back (a 429 with `retryAfterMs`) may be waited out in the same session with `--on-quota wait:<minutes>`, up to that many minutes across the whole run; past the ceiling, or with no time given, it does not retry. Each try is its own `attempt` event.
 - **Request event.** Carries model, effort, `toolsHash`, `systemHash`, `bodyHash`, TTL and header names with value hashes. Never header values.
 - **Role fallback** starts a new session on the fallback model; it never swaps the model inside a session (cache rule 5).
-- **Quota fallback.** A run that ends on a `quota` error continues on its fallback model (`--fallback`, then `fallback` in `~/.cedia/settings.json`, then the built-in `deepseek` → `anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5`; `none` turns it off; a repo cannot set it). The new session has `parentSession`, a logged reminder that the tree may hold part of the work, what is left of the turn and budget limits, and the first session's changed files as writes the done gate must still see verified. The result adds up both sessions' spend and turns.
+- **Quota fallback.** By default a run that ends on a `quota` error continues on its fallback model (`--fallback`, then `fallback` in `~/.cedia/settings.json`, then the built-in `deepseek` → `anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5`; `none` turns it off; a repo cannot set it). The new session has `parentSession`, a logged reminder that the tree may hold part of the work, what is left of the turn and budget limits, and the first session's changed files as writes the done gate must still see verified. The result adds up both sessions' spend and turns. `--on-quota wait:<minutes>` (or `onQuota` in `~/.cedia/settings.json`) waits for a quota that names its reset time in the same session instead, up to that many minutes across the run: each wait is a logged `attempt`, a line on stderr, and ends on SIGTERM. A spent balance names no time and falls back at once.
+- **Refused history.** A `bad_request` or `context_length` error after a session's first accepted request means the provider refused the history itself (a thinking signature, a tool call it cannot read back, a context past the window); cedia never edits history, so resending fails the same way. The run goes on once in a new session on the same model, as a quota fallback does, with `parentSession`, the first session's changed files for the done gate, recall, and a logged reminder; the thread records the session with `why: 'rejected'`, and a resumed thread whose last session was refused starts a new one.
 - **Mid-conversation system prompt.** Appended as a system message when `midConversationSystem` is true, otherwise as a user text block.
 - **Parallel tools.** Calls whose `ToolSpec.effect` is `read` or `network` run in a bounded pool (8 at a time); `write_workspace` and `exec` run alone, as ordering barriers. `tool_intent` events are written in assistant block order; results go back as one batch (Anthropic requires all results of a turn in one user message).
 - **Permission order in the log.** `assistant → permission → tool_intent (only if allowed) → tool_result`. A denied call gets `tool_result{status:'denied'}` and no `tool_intent`.
